<title>USA: TABLE - NFO Research Q2 net rises slightly.</title>
<headline>TABLE - NFO Research Q2 net rises slightly.</headline>
<dateline>GREENWICH, Conn. 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>					   Three Months    Six Months</p>
<p>				 Ended June 30,(1)  Ended June 30,(1)</p>
<p>					   1997    1996    1997    1996</p>
<p> Revenues			   $35,923 $27,827 $67,892 $53,426</p>
<p> Cost of Revenues		  16,440  11,974  31,666  23,572</p>
<p>Selling, General and</p>
<p>   Administrative Expenses(2)  13,414   9,837  25,241  19,352</p>
<p>Depreciation and</p>
<p>   Amortization Expense	   1,219   1,190   2,448   2,376</p>
<p> Operating Income		   4,850   4,826   8,537   8,126</p>
<p> Interest Expense, Net		 74	43	90	76</p>
<p>Equity Interest in Net Loss</p>
<p>   of Joint Venture		   102     136     180     258</p>
<p> Income Before Income Taxes     4,674   4,647   8,267   7,792</p>
<p> Tax Provision			2,140   2,131   3,653   3,587</p>
<p> Net Income			   2,534   2,516   4,614   4,205</p>
<p>Primary Earnings Per</p>
<p>Weighted Average</p>
<p>   Common Share (3)		   .20     .20     .37     .34</p>
<p>Primary Weighted Average</p>
<p>   Shares Outstanding (3)	12,407  12,439  12,357  12,364</p>
<p>(1) Effective April 1, 1997, the Company acquired Prognostics in a transaction which was accounted for as a pooling of interests. Accordingly, all historical financial information has been restated to include the combined financial results of NFO and Prognostics.</p>
<p>(2) Includes, for the three and six month periods ending June 30, 1997, $448,000 or $0.04 per share in transaction costs associated with the Prognostics' pooling of interests.</p>
<p>(3) For comparability, the earnings per share and share data reflect the three-for-two stock split which became effective on February 5, 1996.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
